$************************RELEASE VERSION*********************************** 





$ MatCalc thermodynamic steel database, version 2.059, created 2016-07-26

$

$ This database contains edited and newly assessed thermodynamic data for steel.

$ Thermodynamic parameters have been assessed at TU Wien 

$ by Povoden-Karadeniz Erwin. 

$

$ ##########################################################################

$

$ use with MatCalc version 5.61.0.056 or higher

$

$ ##########################################################################

$ 

$ Copyright holder and editor: Erwin Povoden-Karadeniz 

$ (erwin.povoden-karadeniz@tuwien.ac.at)

$

$ This database mc_fe_v2.059.tdb is made available under the 

$ Open Database License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. 

$ Any rights in individual contents of the database are licensed under the 

$ Database Contents License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1.0/. 

$

$ ##########################################################################





$ The following assessments are incorporated in this database:

$

$ ... see list of publications in the reference section 

$ at the end of this file ...





$ The following elements are included in this database:

$

$ Fe, Al, B, C, Co, Cr, Cu, H, Hf, La, Mn, Mo, N, Nb, Ni, O, P, Pd, S, Si, 

$ Ti, V, W, Y



$ This database has been optimised inside the following limits:

$ Temperature: 673 K - 2000 K

$

$ Alloy composition (wt.%): Al<3  B<0.5  C<0.5  Co<3  Cr<25  Cu<1  Hf<0.5  

$ La<0.5  MN<25  Mo<5  N<1  Nb<1  Ni<26  O<0.5  P<0.005  Pd<4  S<0.5  Si<3.5  

$ Ti<0.5  V<0.5  W<3  Y<0.5 



$ H: Only binary Fe-H parameters in fcc and bcc are edited.



$ Typical applications: 9-12% Cr steels, hot-work tool steels, 

$ microalloyed steels, austenitic stainless steels, PH maraging steels.



$ The following phases are included in this database:

$ They are listed in the order of their appearance in 

$ part D) Thermodynamic model parameters for phases. 

$ For their documentation see part D). 

$ Documentation and priority rankings suggested by the editor are visible 

$ in the MatCalc databases window after reading the database 

$ and marking the phase of interest.

$   

$ LIQUID

$ 

$ FCC_A1 

$ BCC_A2 

$ HCP_A3 

$

$ ALPHA_MN 

$ BETA_MN

$ BETA_RHOMBO_B 

$ DIAMOND_A4

$ GRAPHITE

$

$ Ordered phases (split model used) 

$ BCC_B2 

$

$ Intermetallic phases

$ CHI_A12  CO3MO  CO3V  COV3  CR3MN5  G_PHASE  LAVES_PHASE  MNNI 

$ MNNI2  MNNI_T3  MU_PHASE  MU_PHASE_I  ETA NITI2  R_PHASE  SIGMA  FE17Y2

$ NI5Y  PDFE_L12  PDMN_AF  PDMN_P  PDMN_B2  PD2MN  PD3MN  Pd5MN3  PD6FE5MN2

$

$ Carbides 

$ CEMENTITE  CR2VC2  K_CARB  KSI_CARBIDE  M3C2  M6C  

$ M7C3  M12C  M23C6  MOC_ETA  V3C2  WC  

$   

$ Metastable transition carbides

$ EPS_CARB  ETA_CARB  FE24C10  KSI_FE5C2

$

$ Nitrides

$ ALN  ALN_EQU  BN_HP4  CR3NI2SIN FE4N  MN6N4  MN6N5  MNSIN2  SI3N4  ZET

$

$ Borides

$ CRB  CR2B  CR5B3  FEB  FENBB  FE3NB3B4  M2B  MNB2  MNB4  O_MN2B  MN3B4

$ MOB  MOB2  MO2M1B2  NBB  NB3B2  M5B6  TIB  TIB2  TI3B4

$

$ Sulfides

$ A_CHALC  ANILITE  B_CHALC  COVELLITE  CU2S  DIGENITE

$ DISULF  DJURLEITE  FC_MONO  FC_ORTHO  FES_P  MNS_Q  PYRR  TIS

$  

$ Carbo-sulfides

$ TI4C2S2

$

$ Oxides

$ Simple oxide models without considering of 

$ cation and oxygen nonstoichiometries are used.

$ CORUND  HALITE  HF1O2_M  HF1O2_T  HF1O2_C  LA2O3_A  LA2O3_H  LA2O3_C  SIO2   

$ SPINEL  TI2O3  TIO2  TRID  Y2O3_H  Y2O3_C  YALO3  Y4AL2O9  Y2TIO5  Y2TI2O7 

$

$ Phosphides

$ M2P  M3P

$

$ Special phases

$ BCC_DISL

