$###########################################################################

$                   THERMODYNAMIC PARAMETERS: SIGMA

$###########################################################################

$

 PHASE SIGMA %  3 8   4   18 ! 

$NOTE: In austenitic stainless steels, set Ni% instead of Fe% on sublattice 1.

$Intermetallic transition elements compound with broad solid solubility range. 

$Tetragonal with five non-equivalent sites. 

$A simplified 3-sublattice description is used.  

$Hard and brittle topologically close-packed (TCP) precipitates. 

$Optimized for use in thermokinetic precipitation simulations in 

$austenitic stainless steel (pov12,pov13). For typical austenitic stainless steels 

$(e.g. grade 316) use default mayor constituents :FE%:CR%::

$>> 4 !

